text Once I reply, Yoshino-san quickly climbs up a pole two away from mine.
text This is my first solo job.
text While I've done these things plenty of times before, I still get nervous when I'm left to fend for myself.
text There's a large, drum-like transformer on the pole Yoshino-san climbs up; with jobs like this, we normally check whether or not there are any shorts and if the fuses are all right.
text @[Tomoya]
text Are you okay over there?
sound MUC.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text No problem.
text I'm answered quietly, and I begin working myself.
text First, I need to secure my footing.
text To prevent accidents, telephone poles have their first three or four steps removed.
text I begin by firmly attaching the missing steps.
text I carefully climb up and tie my safety belt to a metal fitting, adjoining myself to the pole.
text This means I won't fall from the thing while working. Even if I somehow happen to slip, I'll just end up hanging mid-air.
text If there's any issue at all, it's that climbing down is difficult.
text That's why I'd normally use the ladder, but Yoshino-san is using it today.
text I carefully begin my usual work.
