text I measure out the opening that's been cut into the distribution panel.
text If we leave the freshly-cut metal board out in the open, it'll begin to corrode, and it could even damage the electric lines that pass through it.
text The bushing is a plastic protective material we use to cover the board.
text I put my knife to the bushing.
text The knife has a marking every centimeter on its blade.
text This is a clever way to save time, because it's inefficient to have to use a separate tool to measure every little thing.
text After measuring it down to around the right centimeter, I cut off the bushing and fill the hole.
text I've done this countless times, and it fits almost perfectly in to the opening.
text @[Tomoya]
text I'm done.
