text ...*Staaare*
text I'm bored. There's nothing to do.
text I see other people doing office work, so I offer to help them as I did before, but they politely turn me down.
text There doesn't seem to be anything for me to do.
text Oh well. I guess I'll just make some tea for now.
sound MV1.aac
text @[Boss]
text Okazaki-kun, a second?
text @[Tomoya]
text Yes, what is it?
sound MV2.aac
text @[Boss]
text Do you have the map and sales slips for today's sites?
text @[Tomoya]
text Oh, yes. I do have them ready just in case.
sound MV3.aac
text @[Boss]
text Do you know what all the part numbers are?
text I take a look at the sales slips stuffed in my shirt pocket.
text There isn't a single number I don't recognize.
text These jobs are all ones I've done before.
text @[Tomoya]
text I think I'll be okay. These are all numbers I remember.
sound MV4.aac
text @[Boss]
text Then you go ahead to the site and start working. I'll send Yoshino your way once I get a hold of him.
text @[Tomoya]
text What? It's pretty far...
text Today's site is a little more than ten kilometers away from where we are now.
sound MV5.aac
text @[Boss]
text I'll drive you over, along with your ladder and all your tools. You shouldn't need any heavy machinery today.
text @[Tomoya]
text Is it really okay for me to do the work on my own?
sound MV6.aac
text @[Boss]
text Yoshino was saying that you seem about ready. Just don't forget to contact us if something happens.
text @[Tomoya]
text All right.
text This is all so sudden that I don't know what to do.
text But one thing I don't feel is anxiety, even though I'm being told I'll need to work solo.
