text Once I arrive at the work site, I see that the street light has already been installed.
text It seems like I only need to do the wiring and testing.
text I bring out a number of plastic-covered parts as well as a reel of cable.
text @[Tomoya]
text Umm, they go out from there, which means...
text I confirm each step of the job as I mumble to myself.
text I don't know when it happened, but I'd remembered everything I have to do.
text I get stuck at a few points, but once I put the parts together, I remember.
text Things I'd failed at in the past.
text Things I hadn't been able to do despite trying over and over again.
text Things I'd remembered after being repeatedly scolded by Yoshino-san.
text They all now connected together.
text I remove my safety belt and climb down the pole.
text All that's left to do is test if the light works.
music ~
text The light is normally controlled automatically by the distribution board, but I flip the test switch I'd installed.
